interpretation:
Slice D adds a deterministic MockBankSandbox Contract Fulfillment Corridor over the validated Root-created Supplier A ActionCommitPacket v0.2 model.

It proves:
- the corridor consumes only the scoped Supplier A packet;
- the corridor validates scope, amount, creditor, payment slot, adapter binding, idempotency, expiry/TTL, and forbidden surfaces;
- the corridor creates mock payment intent, consent, and order as deterministic local structures only;
- the corridor creates and validates mock receipt evidence;
- terminal receipt is observed in local proof-only registry;
- receipt is evidence only;
- receipt does not create permission, FinalOutput, future permission, Supplier B authorization, shipment release, packet-scope mutation, production DRS record, or effects;
- Supplier B remains blocked;
- shipment remains held;
- real bank, supplier, and warehouse APIs are excluded;
- no real payment or real-world effect occurs;
- reasoning does not restart after Root;
- Root remains final authority.

